course: dictionary
lesson: 7284
title: Pinky: a finger and a shade of pink
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word pinky has two main meanings. As a noun, your pinky is the smallest finger on your hand, the little finger. In the USA, Canada, Scotland and Australia people often say pinky, but in England people often say little finger.
explain: Use the words around pinky to work out which meaning fits. «A pinky promise is a children's promise made by hooking little fingers together.» The clue is hooking little fingers, so pinky means the little finger here.
explain: As an adjective, pinky means slightly pink. In «a pinky purple», the word pinky tells you the purple has a touch of pink in it. Check by swapping in your meaning: a slightly pink purple still makes sense.
explain: A pinky promise is a special promise. «A pinky promise is still a promise, and people remember broken ones.» So if you make a pinky promise, you must keep it, just like any other promise.
fact: Pinky, as a noun, means the smallest finger on your hand, the little finger.
fact: A pinky promise is a children's promise made by hooking little fingers together.
fact: Pinky, as an adjective, means slightly pink, as in «a pinky purple».
fact: People in the USA, Canada, Scotland and Australia often say pinky; in England people often say little finger.
fact: A pinky promise is still a promise, and people remember broken ones.
exercise: «A pinky promise is a children's promise made by hooking little fingers together.» What is a pinky promise? | A promise made in a pink room | *A promise made by hooking little fingers together | A promise made with your thumbs | A promise you can break without anyone noticing
exercise: Ruby says, «In England we say little finger, but my cousin in Australia says pinky.» What does pinky mean? | *The smallest finger on your hand | A kind of sweet | The thumb on your hand | A slightly pink colour
exercise: The magazine picture uses «magenta (a pinky purple)». What does pinky mean in this sentence? | A kind of finger | Very dark | Bright sky blue | *Slightly pink
test: «A pinky promise is still a promise, and people remember broken ones.» What does this sentence tell you about a pinky promise? | It can be broken with no one caring | *It must be kept, like any other promise | It does not count if you are joking | It is only for grown-ups
test: Which part of your body does a pinky promise use? | Elbows | Ears | *Little fingers | Big toes
exam: In «a pinky purple», what does pinky mean? | A kind of finger | Very bright | *Slightly pink | A sort of blue
